# Feature 2: SkillRegistry Implementation - COMPLETED

## Summary
Created the SkillRegistry component for skill discovery and wired it to the CLI list command.

## Files Created
- internal/application/skills/registry.go - SkillRegistry implementation
- internal/application/skills/registry_test.go - Comprehensive test suite (13 tests)

## Files Modified
- internal/application/container.go - Added skillRegistry field and SkillRegistry() accessor
- internal/presentation/cli/commands/list.go - Replaced getMockSkills() with loadSkills() using registry

## Implementation Details

### SkillRegistry (internal/application/skills/registry.go)
- Thread-safe caching of loaded skills using sync.RWMutex
- LoadBuiltInSkills() - Loads from ./skills directory (bundled skills)
- LoadUserSkills(dir) - Loads from ~/.skillrunner/skills (user customizations)
- LoadAll() - Loads both built-in and user skills (user skills override built-in)
- GetSkill(id) - Retrieves skill by ID
- GetSkillByName(name) - Retrieves skill by name
- ListSkills() - Returns all loaded skills
- Register/Unregister/Clear - Manual skill management
- Reload() - Clears cache and reloads all skills

### Container Integration
- Added skillRegistry field to Container struct
- Added SkillRegistry() accessor method
- Skills are automatically loaded during container initialization
- Loading errors are silently ignored (skills are optional)

### List Command Changes
- Replaced getMockSkills() with loadSkills()
- loadSkills() retrieves skills from the registry via GetContainer()
- Displays real skill metadata (name, description, phase count, routing profile)

